# Mocking with vi.spyOn or vi.mock

```javascript
import { describe, it, expect, vi } from 'vitest'
import { mount } from '@vue/test-utils'
import UserProfile from './UserProfile.vue'

// Mock global fetch
vi.stubGlobal('fetch', vi.fn(() =>
  Promise.resolve({
    json: () => Promise.resolve({ name: 'John' })
  })
))

it('fetches and displays user', async () => {
  const wrapper = mount(UserProfile, { props: { userId: 1 } })
  await wrapper.vm.$nextTick() // wait for async
  expect(wrapper.text()).toContain('John')
})
```

# Mocking Child Components

Use `global.components` to provide a mock for a child component:

```javascript
const wrapper = mount(Parent, {
  global: {
    components: {
      ChildComponent: {
        template: '<div>Mocked Child</div>'
      }
    }
  }
})
```

To mock provide/inject, use `global.provide`:
```javascript
const wrapper = mount(Component, {
  global: {
    provide: {
      theme: 'dark'
    }
  }
})
```

